MockMic — Capstone Kickoff (Day 1 of 10)
#60DaysOfClaudeAI — Day 51/60
Today marks the start of my 10-day capstone: going from no idea to a deployed v1.0 product, following a real software development lifecycle — Requirements → Design → Setup → Implementation → Testing → Deployment → Maintenance.
The product: MockMic
Practice out loud. Walk in ready.
A voice-first mock interview practice app. Users pick an interview category, answer AI-generated questions out loud (or typed), get instant structured AI feedback, and build confidence through tracked, repeated practice.
Why this project
Interview anxiety rarely comes from not knowing the answer — it comes from never having said it out loud under pressure before. Most prep tools stop at writing better answers on paper. MockMic is built for the part that actually decides outcomes: rehearsing the answer live, and getting honest feedback on how it landed.
Today's process
Instead of jumping straight to building, today was spent as a structured product discovery and sprint-planning session:
Interview-style discovery — one question at a time, narrowing from a broad interest area (career/education) down to a specific, scoped product
Scope protection — actively pushing back on feature creep given a real constraint: ~1–2 hours of build time per day
Explicit v1.0 boundaries — a clear list of what ships and what's intentionally deferred to Future Scope
Deliverables produced today
Product Requirements Document (PRD) — problem statement, target users, goals, in/out-of-scope features, risks, and a Day-10 definition of done
Implementation Blueprint (Days 2–10) — a day-by-day build plan with objectives, step-by-step instructions, files to create, testing tasks, and handoff notes, so each remaining day can start from a fresh AI conversation and continue without re-planning
Pitch Deck — problem, users, solution, key features, technical approach, future scope, and vision
Recommended tech stack (locking on Day 2)
Frontend: HTML/CSS/JavaScript
Voice: Browser-native Web Speech API — free, no install
Auth + database: Firebase free tier
AI: Claude API, called through a serverless proxy
Hosting: Vercel/Netlify free tier
All free-tier, chosen specifically to fit a solo build with limited daily hours.
